			<key>footerText</key>
			<string>VidGrab saves the video you are watching.

A small download button sits in a corner of every video an app plays. Tap it, or hold the video, and choose what to do with it. A bar at the top shows the progress and has a button to cancel.

Downloads asked for while one is running wait in a queue and start one after another. The bar says how many are waiting; its cancel button stops only the one running, and the menu has Clear Queue.

It works with videos an app plays through iOS's own player. Where an app draws its videos itself, no button appears and a hold does nothing.</string>
